.TH CANON-SCAN-TO-PC 1 "2026" "canon-scan-to-pc" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
canon-scan-to-pc \- receive "Scan \(-> Computer" scans from a Canon imageCLASS / i-SENSYS printer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B canon-scan-to-pc
[\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig\fR] [\fB\-v\fR] [\fB\-\-status\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] | \fB\-\-discover\fR | \fB\-\-scan\-now\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Registers this computer in a Canon printer's \fBScan \(-> Computer\fR list (Canon's MFNP
protocol, UDP port 8610) and keeps it there. When this computer is picked on the printer
and Start is pressed, the scan is fetched with SANE's pixma backend and saved, by default
as a PDF in \fI~/Scans\fR. It signs off before the computer sleeps or shuts down.
.PP
It normally runs as the systemd user service \fBcanon-scan-to-pc.service\fR; settings can be
changed with \fBcanon-scan-to-pc-settings\fR(1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIfile\fR
Settings file (default \fI~/.config/canon-scan-to-pc/config.ini\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-status
Show whether the service runs, where it is registered, and the last scan.
.B \-\-json
gives machine-readable output.
.TP
.B \-\-discover
List Canon scanners on the network (needs \fBavahi-browse\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-scan\-now
Scan once with the configured settings, without using the printer's panel.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Debug logging.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/canon-scan-to-pc/config.ini
(an annotated example is in \fI/usr/share/doc/canon-scan-to-pc/config.ini.example\fR)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR canon-scan-to-pc-settings (1),
.BR scanimage (1),
.BR sane-pixma (5)
.PP
https://github.com/anthonytheinventor/canon-scan-to-pc
